Description: Python library and CLI for Debian package metadata
 minideblib is a small Python 3 library for handling Debian source and
 binary packages: control files, changelogs and .dsc files,
 version comparison, and .deb and ar archives. It can also read APT
 repository indexes (Release, Packages, Sources, Contents, DEP-11).
 .
 The package also ships the minideb command, which queries APT
 repositories and inspects .deb and .dsc files. PyYAML (DEP-11) and
 zstandard (.zst indexes) are optional.
